<% consultation_url = PublicProductRscDemoPresenter::CONSULTATION_URL %>
<% native_shakaperf = @presenter.native_shakaperf_benchmark %>

<div class="dd dd-performance">
  <main class="dd-main">
    <header class="dd-header dd-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="dd-eyebrow">VP Engineering brief · actual ShakaPerf CLI</p>
        <h1>Paints 49&ndash;76% faster. Ships 36&ndash;56% more.</h1>
        <p>
          Native RSC product pages paint much sooner and use 93% fewer JavaScript requests, but transfer more bytes and
          respond more slowly. The suite correctly refused to call this an overall win.
        </p>
        <p class="dd-proof-line">
          <strong>Decision:</strong> continue to a bounded pilot. Do not roll out until bundle weight, TTFB, and field
          Web Vitals pass production-parity gates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="dd-actions">
        <a href="<%= rsc_performance_demo_path %>#native-shakaperf-result" class="dd-btn">See every measured number</a>
        <a href="<%= @presenter.native_shakaperf_artifact_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dd-btn">Open raw summary</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="dd-body">
      <%= render "public_product_rsc_demo/native_shakaperf_summary", native_shakaperf:, compact: true %>

      <section class="dd-decision-grid" aria-label="RSC pilot decision">
        <article class="dd-decision-card dd-decision-card--go">
          <p class="dd-eyebrow">Why pilot</p>
          <strong>Buyers see the page sooner</strong>
          <span>FCP -76% · LCP -74% / -49% · CLS -98% / -97%</span>
        </article>
        <article class="dd-decision-card dd-decision-card--hold">
          <p class="dd-eyebrow">Why not rollout</p>
          <strong>Delivery got more expensive</strong>
          <span>JS +206% · bytes +56% / +36% · TTFB +35% / +39%</span>
        </article>
        <article class="dd-decision-card">
          <p class="dd-eyebrow">Causal limit</p>
          <strong>This is an architecture result</strong>
          <span>RSC, server rendering, isolated bundles, and legacy-script omission changed together.</span>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="dd-section" id="pilot-gates">
        <header>
          <p class="dd-eyebrow">Three gates</p>
          <h2>What has to converge before rollout</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="dd-gate-flow">
          <article><span>01</span><strong>Shrink hydration</strong><small>Attack the 2.22 MB client boundary and Microsoft&rsquo;s 199 ms TBT.</small></article>
          <article><span>02</span><strong>Recover server time</strong><small>Remove the 80&ndash;119 ms TTFB regression under matched load.</small></article>
          <article><span>03</span><strong>Prove conversion</strong><small>Run production-parity RUM for LCP, INP, availability, and buyer conversion.</small></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <details class="dd-link-panel">
        <summary>Implementation, rollback, and license boundary</summary>
        <div class="dd-detail-grid">
          <p><strong>Adoption:</strong> one native product route streams through React on Rails Pro while unrelated routes remain on Inertia.</p>
          <p><strong>Operations:</strong> the RSC path adds a Node renderer, a dedicated client/server build, timeout/retry behavior, and stream observability.</p>
          <p><strong>Rollback:</strong> remove <code>rsc=1</code> or route traffic back to the existing Inertia action; the same product data remains available.</p>
          <p><strong>License:</strong> React on Rails is MIT; React on Rails Pro, its renderer, and <code>react-on-rails-rsc</code> are commercial.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <div class="dd-actions">
        <a href="<%= rsc_performance_demo_path %>#native-shakaperf-result" class="dd-btn">Audit the ShakaPerf result</a>
        <a href="<%= consultation_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dd-btn">Plan the bounded pilot</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>
